    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Latino History\ndate: 2021-08-06\n---\nLatino History\n\nLatino history in what is now the United States goes back even before early Spanish colonization. As part of the largest ethnic group in the United States, Latinas and Latinos have significantly contributed to the nation's identity and have played a vital role in shaping American culture. The Latino population in the United States has grown to over 60 million today, leaving a big impact on its democracy, economy, and culture.\n\nFor centuries, Latino culture has influenced all areas of American life, including food, sports, business, politics, science, education, and the arts. Music and dance styles such as salsa and reggaeton have become popular nationwide thanks to artists like Celia Cruz and Bad Bunny. The achievements of legendary athletes like Roberto Clemente and Mariano Rivera have transformed the sports industry. Figures like Supreme Court Justice Sonia Sotomayor have been pioneers in their accomplishments. Artists like Roberto Lugo and Judy Baca draw on their unique experiences to push the boundaries of artistic expression. Artists and performers such as playwright Lin-Manuel Miranda and photographer Laura Aguilar have been strong advocates for increasing the representation of people of color in the entertainment industry. Throughout history, Latinas and Latinos have enriched the cultural landscape of the United States.\n\nWhile continuing to overcome struggles related to prejudice, injustice, racism, sexism, and more, the Latino community has broken barriers and achieved great success. The perseverance, resilience, creativity, dynamism, ingenuity, and more demonstrated throughout Latino history serves as inspiration and have paved the way for future generations of Latinas and Latinos.\n\nTo learn more about how Latino history is American history and its continued impact on the United States, explore some of our online resources:\n\n- Early Latino History: Discover the complex and diverse Latino history that has shaped the United States since its founding.\n\n- Latino Civil Rights: Throughout the history of the United States, the Latino community has faced injustices. Learn about the ongoing fight for Latino civil rights.\n\n- Latino Culture: Explore how Latino culture has contributed to society and culture in the United States.\n\n- Latino Art: See how Latino art and artists have shaped American culture through a range of creative art forms, such as music, painting, and pottery.\n\n- Latino Immigration: Learn about how the history and unique stories of Latino immigrants have contributed to the culture of the United States.\n\n- Latinos in the United States: Explore how the diverse Latino community continues to be an integral part of the United States' identity.\n\n"
