pecially sugar, European colonial expansion and slavery would remain linked into the 1800s. The use of exile to penal colonies would also continue.\n\nThe European \"discovery\" of the New World, as named by Amerigo Vespucci in 1503, opened another colonial chapter, beginning with the colonization of the Caribbean in 1493 with Hispaniola (later to become Haiti and the Dominican Republic). The Portuguese and Spanish Empires were the first global empires because they were the first to stretch across different continents (discounting"
